      "severity": "P1",
      "title": "Failed first traditional render could enable confirmation and delete stored raw credentials",
      "reproduction": "Existing raw credential + initial dynamic loginUi failure left fields/values empty. Prior toolbar confirmation reached the accepted empty-map form action, which removes raw login info.",
      "lockedEvidence": "SourceLoginDialog.kt:669-672 requires !isRenderingLoginUi && rowUis != null; a failed initial parse has no valid rowUis.",
      "fixEvidence": "BookSourceFormLoginView.swift:109/121 toolbar disabled; doLogin:554 guard; submitForm:590 captured hadValidOriginalForm checked after classification. originalFormLoaded becomes true only after a successful complete render, including valid []. Failed later render keeps old fields/values/loaded state; generation and cancellation checks precede apply/catch.",
      "verificationBoundary": "Exact source/control-flow inspection and Swift grammar. The new Swift guards have no actual SDK/UI execution here."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P2",
      "title": "Nil or explicitly empty selector options changed original control semantics",
      "reproduction": "Nil original select/toggle chars projected to [], and the shared Grid turned an original empty selector into a text input. Original nil chars has type-specific placeholders; explicit [] remains a selection control.",
      "lockedEvidence": "SourceLoginDialog.kt:452 and 578 retain distinct null/empty chars; select row is always a selector.",
      "fixEvidence": "LegadoOriginalLoginUIForm uses type-specific nil placeholders after null filtering, preserving explicit []. Grid only uses the former empty-options TextField when originalRowID == nil. Existing JVM static method exercises nil select/toggle and explicit []+default; existing App method asserts projection.",
      "verificationBoundary": "Actual JVM vector assertions passed in the four-method XML. App assertions are defined and grammar checked, not SDK executed."
    },
    {
      "severity": "P2",
      "title": "Shared control display filtered empty choices, invented an undeclared choice, or replaced an explicit empty working value",
      "reproduction": "chars=[\"\",\"signed\"], working value=\"\" displayed signed while confirmation still submitted empty. An undeclared stored/default value was added to the choices. The original toggle also filtered empty chars and could use a selector instead of its cyclic button.",
      "lockedEvidence": "SourceLoginDialog.kt:452/462/469 uses exact null-filtered chars and indexOf; ViewExtensions.kt:489-493 clamps index to a real adapter position. Toggle keeps all declared chars and its initialized working value.",
      "fixEvidence": "v2 LoginManager.originalSelectionDisplayValue matches an existing choice or clamps display to first without modifying the working map. Grid original branch retains every declared choice, assigns position-based stable view IDs, appends no extra value, preserves empty chars, always uses toggle pill, and reads toggle working value directly. Legacy/TTS nil-originalRowID branches retain previous filtering/fallback. Existing App method adds empty/unmatched/clamped assertions.",
      "verificationBoundary": "Final exact Swift source and existing test-definition inspection plus 12 grammar roots. No actual SwiftUI display acceptance or new Kotlin/JAR rebuild was claimed because all four production Kotlin, manifest and JVM test bytes stayed exact."
